Author:&nbsp;<a href="/showmember.php?name=Sureall">Sureall</a>&nbsp;(---.delta.com)<br>
Date:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;03-28-01 01:05<br>
<br><HTML>Hmm seems pretty silly to let a couple of morons dictate what ye should do, best to ignore em Im thinking, life on EQ is pretty simple really, if ye like the game stay, if ye like the guild stay, I personally like both so tis a simple thing for me. <br>
<br>
The fact is that obviously it was agreed by many that what they were doing was wrong and they were kicked out because of it. Im new to the guild so tis true that Im not knowing the two in question, but seems pretty clear to me that if someone or some people commit an act that harms an individual or individuals, how in the world can thier actions be the fault of the victims?<br>
<br>
Well im rambling now..one of me flaws it seems, but what it boils down to is...The world is full of idiots, but ye cant be letting them make yer decisions for you, they are idiots after all...so think and decide what you want to do and remember, theres more than just those two in the guild...is anyone asking you to leave? <br>
Why should those two be considered a reflection on the rest of us? <br>
<br>
Ultimatly you have to make the decision, but is that decision what you truly want or some misconception of what you think others feel? Move on get past this thing and forget it, doesnt seem worth remembering to me anyways.</HTML></font></tt><p>
